<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Southern Cross half yr profit falls.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Southern Cross half yr profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year to December 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     6.95 vs  7.91</p>
<p>    Net					4.50 vs  5.65</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    14.0  vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Sales				   44.64 vs 43.78</p>
<p>    Other income			   1.40 vs  1.15</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   17.0  vs 23.0</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			  nil vs  nil</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date March 27  </p>
<p>Reg date March 17</p>
<p>    Tax					2.45 vs 2.26</p>
<p>    Interest				 2.75 vs 2.92</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   2.89 vs 2.66</p>
<p>NOTE: Southern Cross Broadcasting (Australia) Ltd is an operator of commercial television and radio stations.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
